    {
        "content": "<p><del>Shouldn’t the result type of dualFamily should be <code>Finset (Finset α)</code>?</del></p>",
        "id": 590909488,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1777152420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Never mind. I thought you might want to preserve the mapping from specific x to sets containing it.</p>",
        "id": 590909822,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1777152694
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My next review is simple. You should separate out the definition and lemmas of the encoding. Also is this proof AI generated?  This is a very typical thing for AI to do, namely generate internal definitions inside a proof. If yes, then this should be acknowledged. We have some policies about AI submissions for new contributors.</p>",
        "id": 590909922,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1777152855
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The encoding definition should not be <code>@[expose]</code>d</p>",
        "id": 590909955,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1777152898
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"466334\">Shreyas Srinivas</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Assouad.27s.20dual.20VC.20bound/near/590909922\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My next review is simple. You should separate out the definition and lemmas of the encoding. Also is this proof AI generated?  This is a very typical thing for AI to do, namely generate internal definitions inside a proof. If yes, then this should be acknowledged. We have some policies about AI submissions for new contributors.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I wrote the proof myself, after our discussion and your guidance on contributing to mathlib Shreyas. The proof from the PR you are referring to requires a cardinality argument <code>(Bool^(d+1)) = 2^(d+1)</code>, a bijection to<code> Fin(2^(d+1))</code> then use of condition 2^(d+1) less than or equals S, a bijection of <code>Fin|S|</code> to <code>↥S</code> finally using all of this to write the injection term. (And, an injectivity of that injection argument to recover the bitstring from a codeword) <br>\nIn my initial naive attempt, I ended up defining multiple trivial items which individually noted all of these composition steps . <br>\nThen I realized I can club some of the steps (like equivalence, embed, inject) into a single cube embedding composition. I mostly did not extract it out to file scope because I procrastinated on the pending round of changes (from cube b to something like cubeEmbedding S hcard b) in various places, which I decided to postpone and subsequenty slipped my mind as a pending task. (mostly because this composition and the encoding lemmas are mostly very specific to the proof, so I thought it was a very low priority item per my understanding) </p>\n<p>Will make the change you suggested.</p>",
        "id": 590962486,
        "sender_full_name": "Dhruv Gupta",
        "timestamp": 1777203548
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay. Then no AI ack needed.</p>",
